// Pixie's Unstable Mixture Ascension - reworked from pure numeric scaling ("+X% death-explosion
// damage/radius per rank") into a build-defining rhythm: an explosion that KILLS something empowers
// her NEXT explosion, up to a small stack cap, and at max stacks that empowered blast splits into a
// second delayed shockwave.
//
// Lives on Pixie herself, granted/refreshed by UnstableMixturePassiveUpgradeData.
//
// Proc-recursion safety is the load-bearing part of this line, and is handled entirely through the
// codebase's existing explosion source tagging rather than a bespoke guard:
//  - Stacks are GAINED only from a kill dealt by a genuine, non-chained explosion (see
//    DamageUtility.ApplyDamage's isExplosion/isChainedExplosion pair). A death-explosion chaining
//    into another death-explosion is already tagged isChainedExplosion, so a chain reaction can't
//    farm stacks off itself.
//  - Stacks are SPENT only by a genuine, non-chained explosion too (see
//    DemolitionMasteryUtility.ResolveExplosionEmpowerment, called once per blast from
//    HitEffectUtility.ApplyInRadius/ApplyDamageInRadius).
//  - The rank 3 secondary blast fires with isChainedExplosion: true, so by both rules above it can
//    neither consume empowerment nor generate more of it - it is a payout, never a new link.
component UnstableMixtureUpgrade
{
    // Per-stack bonuses applied to the empowered explosion.
    FP DamageBonusPerStack;
    FP RadiusBonusPerStack;

    // How many stacks can be banked at once - 1 at rank 1, 2 at rank 2+ (the "can stack up to 2"
    // rank). Stacks hold at this ceiling rather than overflowing.
    Byte MaxStacks;
    Byte Stacks;

    // Rank 3 only - when an empowered explosion goes off at MaxStacks, schedule a second, smaller
    // blast shortly afterwards at the same point. 0 SecondaryDamagePercent (ranks 1-2/unpicked)
    // schedules nothing.
    FP SecondaryDamagePercent;
    FP SecondaryRadiusMultiplier;
    FP SecondaryDelay;
}
